The op-log and the operation DAG are append-only, and gc rooted from all
of both, so nothing a rewrite orphaned could ever be collected: a repo
that committed its build output once carried it forever, and gc reported
kilobytes of garbage against gigabytes on disk. Operations now stop
pinning content past gc.retain, default 30d. Branch refs are still marked
unconditionally, so committed history is never at risk whatever its age.

